Read disk images through HFSExplorer's Java file stream on Windows too.

On Windows, DmgFileReader opened the image with HFSExplorer's
WindowsLowLevelIO, which loads llio_amd64.dll: a 2008 Visual C++ build
checked in without its source. That class exists to read raw drives,
which Java cannot open on Windows; a disk image is an ordinary file, and
ReadableFileStream, used on every other system and already here for the
UDIF header, reads it. The llio libraries are deleted in prepare(), so
their lines leave the certification manifest.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

